---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const recoverRequirementsResult = await recoverRequirements(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const resolveAssetsResult = await resolveAssets(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, recoverRequirementsResult.accepted);
const matchArtifactsResult = await matchArtifacts(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, resolveAssetsResult.accepted);
const planClosureResult = await planClosure(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, matchArtifactsResult.accepted);
const assembleDossierResult = await assembleDossier(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, planClosureResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { recoverRequirements: recoverRequirementsResult, resolveAssets: resolveAssetsResult, matchArtifacts: matchArtifactsResult, planClosure: planClosureResult, assembleDossier: assembleDossierResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...recoverRequirementsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...resolveAssetsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...matchArtifactsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...planClosureResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...assembleDossierResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...recoverRequirementsResult.checks, ...resolveAssetsResult.checks, ...matchArtifactsResult.checks, ...planClosureResult.checks, ...assembleDossierResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A manual covers several variants: mark the installed variant and relevant sections. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (mark the installed variant and relevant sections.) through the existing stage result for HandoverRequirement; preserve exact source/version and the prior HandoverRequirement, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A certificate names the wrong asset: block matching despite a familiar model number. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (block matching despite a familiar model number.) through the existing stage result for HandoverRequirement; preserve exact source/version and the prior HandoverRequirement, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — A contractor portal link will expire: archive permitted deliverables with durable hashes. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (archive permitted deliverables with durable hashes.) through the existing stage result for HandoverRequirement; preserve exact source/version and the prior HandoverRequirement, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — Facilities staff cannot open a file format: provide an approved accessible export. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (provide an approved accessible export.) through the existing stage result for HandoverRequirement; preserve exact source/version and the prior HandoverRequirement, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A temporary arrangement expires after handover: transfer the follow-up obligation explicitly. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (transfer the follow-up obligation explicitly.) through the existing stage result for HandoverRequirement; preserve exact source/version and the prior HandoverRequirement, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, recoverRequirements: recoverRequirementsResult, resolveAssets: resolveAssetsResult, matchArtifacts: matchArtifactsResult, planClosure: planClosureResult, assembleDossier: assembleDossierResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
